So indexing helps us to optimize the search of data from the tables in MySQL.
There are two types of indexing: 


1) Clustered Indexing: where we index the primary key of the table to become the index. 


2) Non-clustered Index: where the table does not have a primary key so index to a column where there is somewhat similarity to group by but there is no unique primary key so it will be like group by.


And the syntax for creating indexes is by 

CREATE INDEX idx_product_name on sakila.sales_data(product_name);

Now we talk about Natural Key and Surrogate key.

Surrogate keys are replaced when you leave the organization and then your employee ID is given to the new joinee. 

But even when you die your SSN number is always unique to your own identity so it is a Natural key.

Natural Keys are forever assigned. 

Surrogate keys are temporary. 

primary key --surrogate key 

So basically these are the options we can consider while creating a primary key.

All Natural keys are primary keys by default. But not all Primary keys might be Natural keys as they could be surrogate keys as well. 

